{
"segments": [
{
"s": 0.0,
"e": 10.08,
"text": "Welcome to the Breath Reset. Today we're going to practice Breathe Light, learning to breathe a little quieter, softer, and more comfortably."
},
{
"s": 11.1,
"e": 17.4,
"text": "We'll measure our BOLT score before and after, just to notice whether anything changes. Let's begin."
},
{
"s": 18.98,
"e": 22.24,
"text": "Take a few natural breaths through your nose."
},
{
"s": 24.62,
"e": 34.16,
"text": "On my cue, you're going to be taking one more inhale, and after the exhale, I want you to pinch your nose, and the timer will start on the screen."
},
{
"s": 35.42,
"e": 40.62,
"text": "Stop at the first clear urge to breathe, then return to normal breathing."
},
{
"s": 42.28,
"e": 48.74,
"text": "Ready? Inhale. Exhale. And begin."
},
{
"s": 48.74,
"e": 48.98,
"text": "Ready?"
},
{
"s": 78.74,
"e": 85.62,
"text": "Now make a note of your score, and allow your breathing to return completely to normal."
},
{
"s": 86.96,
"e": 95.64,
"text": "Gently close your eyes if that feels comfortable. Feel your body supported beneath you."
},
{
"s": 96.5,
"e": 103.76,
"text": "Allow your shoulders to soften, your jaw to relax, and simply notice your breathing."
},
{
"s": 105.06,
"e": 116.32,
"text": "Don't change anything just yet. Just notice where you feel the movement. Your chest, your lower ribs, your abdomen."
},
{
"s": 118.06,
"e": 120.1,
"text": "Can you hear yourself breathing?"
},
{
"s": 124.12,
"e": 130.38,
"text": "Does it feel easy? Or is there a little more effort than you need?"
},
{
"s": 137.92,
"e": 146.06,
"text": "Now if it feels comfortable, allow your breathing to become a little softer, a little quieter."
},
{
"s": 147.2,
"e": 154.72,
"text": "There's no need to take big breaths, and no need to push the air out."
},
{
"s": 155.72,
"e": 162.24,
"text": "Just see whether you can let go of any unnecessary effort."
},
{
"s": 175.16,
"e": 181.1,
"text": "Bring your attention to the sensation of air moving through your nostrils."
},
{
"s": 182.1,
"e": 190.1,
"text": "Notice the slightly cooler air as you breathe in, and the slightly warmer air as you breathe out."
},
{
"s": 198.06,
"e": 205.94,
"text": "Allow the inhale to arrive gently, and the exhale to happen naturally."
},
{
"s": 206.94,
"e": 212.72,
"text": "Quiet, soft, and comfortable."
},
{
"s": 217.72,
"e": 229.34,
"text": "Notice your shoulders, your neck, and your jaw, and see whether there's anywhere you can soften a little more."
},
{
"s": 231.64,
"e": 236.5,
"text": "Allow your lower ribs to move comfortably with each breath."
},
{
"s": 241.36,
"e": 251.0,
"text": "You might notice your breathing becoming quieter, or perhaps it hasn't changed very much. Both are fine."
},
{
"s": 252.92,
"e": 259.0,
"text": "Simply exploring what comfortable, effortless breathing feels like."
},
{
"s": 262.4,
"e": 270.98,
"text": "And if you notice yourself trying too hard, see whether you can do a little less. Let your body breathe."
},
{
"s": 283.4,
"e": 291.08,
"text": "Now let go of any attempt to change your breathing. Allow your breathing to find its own natural rhythm."
},
{
"s": 292.36,
"e": 297.74,
"text": "Nothing to achieve, nothing to measure. Just notice."
},
{
"s": 300.28,
"e": 306.16,
"text": "How does your breathing feel? Perhaps it's a little quieter."
},
{
"s": 307.16,
"e": 317.56,
"text": "Perhaps your body feels settled, or perhaps nothing has changed. Whatever you notice is fine."
},
{
"s": 322.16,
"e": 328.0,
"text": "Now we're going to repeat our bolt measurement. Take a few normal breaths."
},
{
"s": 328.8,
"e": 337.56,
"text": "On my cue, we're going to be taking one more inhale, and exhale, then gently pinch our nose and watch the timer."
},
{
"s": 338.76,
"e": 345.42,
"text": "Stop at the first clear urge to breathe, then release and return to normal breathing."
},
{
"s": 347.02,
"e": 353.56,
"text": "Take a nice big inhale, exhale, and begin."
},
{
"s": 358.0,
"e": 364.24,
"text": "Now make a note of your second score. Was it higher, lower, or about the same?"
},
{
"s": 366.08,
"e": 374.78,
"text": "Remember, the goal isn't to achieve a particular number. It's to become more aware of your breathing and learn how to make it comfortable and efficient."
},
{
"s": 375.88,
"e": 383.28,
"text": "As you go through your day, notice whether you're breathing with more effort than you need. And if it feels comfortable, allow it to soften."
},
{
"s": 383.28,
"e": 387.86,
"text": "Sometimes breathing better is simply about doing less."
}
],
